+## 8. D1/r3 ownership correction and discriminating proof
+
+The first p03 actual production creation/deletion run reached the parent delete and failed on
+agent_publication_requests_company_id_agent_id_fkey. Every production-created published agent
+has such an immutable owned request. D1/r2's instruction to change only agent_revisions' owner
+cascade therefore made its own unused-deletion criterion impossible. Retained evidence:
+B1-agent-direct-tests1.txt and B1-delete-owned-fks.txt. This is a required ownership correction,
+not permission to delete external publication consumers.
+
+Native ownership follows the existing agent_active_revisions and agent_revision_bindings pattern:
+the request's agent FK cascades on the actual parent deletion, and its immutable trigger permits
+only that parent teardown. Both request→revision FKs stay unchanged; so do all other incoming
+revision, workflow-version, history, run, manifest, role and capability constraints. The responsible
+application deletion transaction still owns company→agent→principal locks, current direct-thread/run
+refusal, reply-selection clear, direct-binding removal and principal retirement. No receipt may be
+removed merely to make a still-live agent's deletion possible. Any retained outside reference aborts
+the full transaction and restores addresses, settings, endpoints, bindings, ownership and request rows.
+
+Required focused proof: production-created unused agent can be deleted and removes its own request,
+revision and owned workflow; standalone request mutation/deletion is refused while the agent lives;
+native same-agent/tenant request result references still refuse invalid rows; retained external
+workflow publication/manifest/history/direct-thread/run consumers refuse deletion with exact unchanged
+resource inventory. Keep original both-order admission/delete race and competing-claimant obligations.
+Inspect the full native incoming FK inventory against this narrow delta. No dependent owner-FK or
+immutable-guard edit is permitted until independent explicit PASS of this revision. Independent notice,
+relay, test-fixture and other unchanged-contract work may continue while this gate is pending, but
+source is frozen for the review assignment identity.
